was eventually destroyed in the fighting, with most of its surviving troops entering Soviet captivity, while a few were evacuated via the Frisches Haff.","LocalizedString":"The 101st Infantry Regiment was a component of the 14th Infantry Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. In 1939 the division was deployed to Poland during the invasion. After the Polish campaign, the division was transferred to the Western Front, where it participated in the invasion of France in 1940. In 1941 the division was assigned to the Ninth Army and Army Group Centre and during Operation Barbarossa, the division was involved in the encirclement of Minsk. In 1943 the division suffered heavy losses during the Battles of Rzhev and during the defense against the Soviet summer counter-offensive called Operation Suvorov.. In 1944, the division was transferred to 3rd Panzer Army and was used as a reserve formation by Army Group Centre. The division was rushed into the line in a desperate attempt to hold back the breakthrough of several Soviet divisions during Operation Bagration, where again it suffered heavy losses and only a handful of troops were able to retreat to the German lines. By the end of the year, the remainder of the division was transferred to the Second Army and were in the area of Ostrolenka, Poland. During the Soviet East Prussian Offensive of January 1945, the rebuilt 14th Infantry Division was pushed north and trapped in the Heiligenbeil pocket, where it attempted a breakout before falling back on Braunsberg. The division was eventually destroyed in the fighting, with most of its surviving troops entering Soviet captivity, while a few were evacuated via the Frisches Haff."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAttacks"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Pincer"],"hasPincer":true,"soundBlowUp":{"Objec